---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'November 2026';

const webPageSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  name: 'Terms of Service & Marketplace Disclaimer | ListLift',
  url: 'https://listlift.com/terms',
  dateModified: '2026-11-22',
  description:
    'ListLift Terms of Service covering acceptable use, seller verification responsibility for generated drafts, SaaS liability limits, and marketplace non-affiliation.',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service & Marketplace Disclaimer"
  description="ListLift Terms of Service: acceptable use, seller verification duty for AI-generated drafts, SaaS liability limits, and marketplace non-affiliation."
  canonicalPath="/terms"
  jsonLd={webPageSchema}
>
  <article class="container legal-shell">
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><span aria-current="page">Terms of Service</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="legal-header">
      <span class="badge badge-pass">Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
      <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="muted legal-intro">
        By accessing or using the ListLift web application or the ListLift Chrome &amp; Edge Extension operated by <strong>[Your Company Legal Name, City, Country]</strong>, you agree to these Terms of Service.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="card legal-body">
      <section>
        <h2>1. Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
        <p>You agree to use ListLift lawfully and responsibly. You may not:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Upload or generate listings for illegal, counterfeit, stolen, hazardous, or marketplace-prohibited products.</li>
          <li>Upload images, trademarks, or text that infringe any third party's intellectual property or publicity rights.</li>
          <li>Use automated bots, scripts, or rotating proxies to scrape ListLift, overwhelm our servers, or bypass free-tier daily rate limits.</li>
          <li>Reverse-engineer, resell, or redistribute access to our backend API without written authorization.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We reserve the right to suspend or terminate access without refund if an account violates this Acceptable Use Policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>2. Generated Drafts &amp; Seller Responsibility Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          All titles, bullet points, descriptions, tags, backend search terms, SKUs, and seller-portal fields generated by ListLift are <strong>automated suggestions and starting drafts</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>You, the seller, are solely responsible</strong> for reviewing and verifying all factual product specifications (dimensions, materials, pack counts, certifications, safety warnings, country of origin), trademark/IP rights, and current marketplace policies before publishing any listing. ListLift does not guarantee search rankings, impressions, conversions, or sales outcomes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>3. Subscriptions, Billing &amp; Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Paid subscriptions are billed in advance on a monthly or annual basis via our authorized payment processors (such as Paddle, Lemon Squeezy, Stripe, or Razorpay). You may cancel anytime before your next renewal date. Full details on eligibility and processing timelines are covered in our <a href="/refunds">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>4. "As-Is" Service &amp; Limitation of Liability</h2>
        <p>
          ListLift is provided on an <strong>"as-is" and "as-available"</strong> basis without warranties of any kind, express or implied. Because third-party marketplaces frequently change their portal layouts and listing rules, we do not guarantee uninterrupted uptime or permanent compatibility with every external form layout.
        </p>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, <strong>[Your Company Legal Name, City, Country]</strong> and its team shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or special damages, including marketplace account suspensions, listing suppressions, lost profits, or temporary API downtime. Our total cumulative liability for any claim arising from your use of ListLift is limited to the amount you paid us in the 12 months preceding the claim.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>5. Third-Party Marketplace Non-Affiliation</h2>
        <p>
          Amazon, Etsy, eBay, Shopify, Walmart, Flipkart, Meesho, and Shopee are trademarks of their respective owners. <strong>ListLift is an independent software tool and is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by any of these marketplaces.</strong>
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>6. Changes &amp; Contact</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms as our platform evolves. Continued use after updates constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms. Questions? Email <a href="mailto:[support@yourdomain.com]">[support@yourdomain.com]</a> or visit our <a href="/contact">Contact page</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-shell {
    padding-top: var(--space-8);
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .legal-header {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  .legal-header h1 {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .legal-intro {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  .legal-body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 24px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 3vw, 34px);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .legal-body h2 {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    font-size: 1.22rem;
  }
  .legal-body p {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal-body p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .legal-body ul {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .legal-body strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
